etting is syntactically valid (yum parses config without error) and that curl's installed version is unaffected. Completed the mandatory single-node restart: captured pre-restart boot_id/uptime baseline, restarted node1 via sudo reboot, polled until reachable, confirmed a new boot_id (proving an actual restart, not just elapsed time), and re-verified post-restart that curl's version and the yum.conf exclude=curl hold both persisted, with the node reporting systemctl is-system-running = running.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected node1 OS/package manager (RHEL 7.9, yum) and current curl version (curl-7.29.0-59.el7.x86_64)\",\"Checked for yum-plugin-versionlock; found it not installed and no enabled yum repos to install it from\",\"Added exclude=curl to /etc/yum.conf [main] section (after backing up the original file) as the native yum hold mechanism\",\"Verified yum parses the new config without error and curl version is unchanged\",\"Captured pre-restart baseline: boot_id, uptime -s, systemctl is-system-running\",\"Rebooted node1 via sudo -n /sbin/reboot (backgrounded so the ack returned before disconnect)\",\"Polled node1 until exec access returned\",\"Confirmed boot_id changed (33b0e84c... -> 27b0bcd3...) and uptime reset, proving an actual reboot occurred\",\"Post-restart: verified curl version unchanged and exclude=curl still present in /etc/yum.conf, and systemctl is-system-running = running\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Baseline: current curl version and no pre-existing hold mechanism\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-0c7f06b61c4743bf\",\"cmd-46464d1c0df44bb9\",\"cmd-055cabc22aec4cc0\"],\"summary\":\"rpm -q curl shows curl-7.29.0-59.el7.x86_64; yum-plugin-versionlock not installed; zero enabled repos (repolist: 0), confirming versionlock plugin install is not possible offline\"},{\"requirement\":\"Applied version hold for curl\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-235e508a33b24bad\",\"cmd-75838a9ffc0a44c0\"],\"summary\":\"Backed up /etc/yum.conf, inserted exclude=curl under [main], confirmed with grep that the line is present\"},{\"requirement\":\"Hold configuration is valid and curl unaffected\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-815f359a616741a4\",\"cmd-ca5fe044f7504a6b\",\"cmd-766cf31e0be14de0\"],\"summary\":\"yum check-update parses config without erroring on the exclude line (only reports no enabled repos); yum.conf content confirmed with exclude=curl present; rpm -q curl still reports the original version\"},{\"requirement\":\"Pre-restart healthy baseline and boot identity for node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-2ec14626dd7e4fc9\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id 33b0e84c-4dd1-406a-8f89-2e8ceca97bd6, uptime -s 2026-08-26 10:34:49, systemctl is-system-running=running, and exclude=curl + curl version confirmed healthy immediately before restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"Restart acknowledgement and disconnect during reboot\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-bda4d2aac3dc4051\",\"cmd-84f3592c544e4b73\",\"cmd-e3a59502cbdf4ddc\"],\"summary\":\"Backgrounded sudo reboot command acknowledged; subsequent exec calls timed out connecting to node1, confirming the node went down for restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"Changed boot identity proving actual restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d15d59105a67429c\"],\"summary\":\"Post-restart boot_id is 27b0bcd3-461a-48fb-99d1-906c694d7785 (different from baseline 33b0e84c...) with fresh uptime 2026-09-29 10:36:04, proving a real reboot occurred\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart recovery of curl version hold and node health\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-03c98801378a4865\"],\"summary\":\"After restart: rpm -q curl still curl-7.29.0-59.el7.x86_64, exclude=curl still present in /etc/yum.conf, systemctl is-system-running=running\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Held curl at its current version (curl-7.29.0-59.el7.x86_64) on node1 by adding `exclude=curl` to /etc/yum.conf [main], the native RHEL7/yum mechanism to prevent a package from being touched by `yum update`. yum-plugin-versionlock could not be installed because node1 has no enabled repos (offline), so the built-in exclude directive was used instead. Verified the setting is syntactically valid (yum parses config without error) and that curl's installed version is unaffected. Completed the mandatory single-node restart: captured pre-restart boot_id/uptime baseline, restarted node1 via sudo reboot, polled until reachable, confirmed a new boot_id (proving an actual restart, not just elapsed time), and re-verified post-restart that curl's version and the yum.conf exclude=curl hold both persisted, with the node reporting systemctl is-system-running = running.","actions_performed":["Inspected node1 OS/package manager (RHEL 7.9, yum) and current curl version (curl-7.29.0-59.el7.x86_64)","Checked for yum-plugin-versionlock; found it not installed and no enabled yum repos to install it from","Added exclude=curl to /etc/yum.conf [main] section (after backing up the original file) as the native yum hold mechanism","Verified yum parses the new config without error and curl version is unchanged","Captured pre-restart baseline: boot_id, uptime -s, systemctl is-system-running","Rebooted node1 via sudo -n /sbin/reboot (backgrounded so the ack returned before disconnect)","Polled node1 until exec access returned","Confirmed boot_id changed (33b0e84c... -> 27b0bcd3...) and uptime reset, proving an actual reboot occurred","Post-restart: verified curl version unchanged and exclude=curl still present in /etc/yum.conf, and systemctl is-system-running = running"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Baseline: current curl version and no pre-existing hold mechanism","command_ids":["cmd-0c7f06b61c4743bf","cmd-46464d1c0df44bb9","cmd-055cabc22aec4cc0"],"summary":"rpm -q curl shows curl-7.29.0-59.el7.x86_64; yum-plugin-versionlock not installed; zero enabled repos (repolist: 0), confirming versionlock plugin install is not possible offline"},{"requirement":"Applied version hold for curl","command_ids":["cmd-235e508a33b24bad","cmd-75838a9ffc0a44c0"],"summary":"Backed up /etc/yum.conf, inserted exclude=curl under [main], confirmed with grep that the line is present"},{"requirement":"Hold configuration is valid and curl unaffected","command_ids":["cmd-815f359a616741a4","cmd-ca5fe044f7504a6b","cmd-766cf31e0be14de0"],"summary":"yum check-update parses config without erroring on the exclude line (only reports no enabled repos); yum.conf content confirmed with exclude=curl present; rpm -q curl still reports the original version"},{"requirement":"Pre-restart healthy baseline and boot identity for node1","command_ids":["cmd-2ec14626dd7e4fc9"],"summary":"Captured boot_id 33b0e84c-4dd1-406a-8f89-2e8ceca97bd6, uptime -s 2026-08-26 10:34:49, systemctl is-system-running=running, and exclude=curl + curl version confirmed healthy immediately before restart"},{"requirement":"Restart acknowledgement and disconnect during reboot","command_ids":["cmd-bda4d2aac3dc4051","cmd-84f3592c544e4b73","cmd-e3a59502cbdf4ddc"],"summary":"Backgrounded sudo reboot command acknowledged; subsequent exec calls timed out connecting to node1, confirming the node went down for restart"},{"requirement":"Changed boot identity proving actual restart","command_ids":["cmd-d15d59105a67429c"],"summary":"Post-restart boot_id is 27b0bcd3-461a-48fb-99d1-906c694d7785 (different from baseline 33b0e84c...) with fresh uptime 2026-09-29 10:36:04, proving a real reboot occurred"},{"requirement":"Post-restart recovery of curl version hold and node health","command_ids":["cmd-03c98801378a4865"],"summary":"After restart: rpm -q curl still curl-7.29.0-59.el7.x86_64, exclude=curl still present in /etc/yum.conf, systemctl is-system-running=running"}]},"ttft_ms":2516,"type":"result","duration_ms":229284,"uuid":"7799a247-34d8-4420-86c5-a8dfe9810615","ttft_stream_ms":1830,"time_to_request_ms":399,"first_content_frame_ms":1831,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
